    "negative_clarification": "Credit-claiming does NOT occur when a senator discusses general policy positions, critiques others' actions, or expresses opinions without linking their personal efforts to a specific outcome. It also does not include instances where the senator is merely reporting on an event, legislation, or funding without explicitly or implicitly taking personal credit for it. The absence of personal agency (e.g., 'I,' 'my,' or 'our' in the context of direct involvement) is a key indicator of non-credit-claiming.",
